{"choices":[{"message":{"content":"{\n  \"status\": \"access_plan\",\n  \"material_requests\": [\n    {\n      \"access_id\": \"source_materials[2].deep_read_material\",\n      \"reason\": \"验证 U1 中跨队列异质性统计依据（PERMANOVA 队列效应解释方差、留一法交叉验证 AUC-ROC 0.59-0.60）的具体数据\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"access_id\": \"source_materials[7].study_summary_A\",\n      \"reason\": \"核实 U1 中菌株级签名在联合免疫治疗中泛癌种预测力但在单药队列失效的具体证据（P0015）\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"access_id\": \"source_materials[11].study_summary_A\",\n      \"reason\": \"确认 U1 中 mCRPC 患者 A. muciniphila 丰度与 ICI 疗效负相关的反例数据（P0270）\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"access_id\": \"source_materials[15].study_summary_A\",\n      \"reason\": \"验证 U1 中波兰队列 F. prausnitzii 高丰度与非响应者相关的特异性发现（P0545）\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"access_id\": \"source_materials[4].local_passages\",\n      \"reason\": \"核实 U2 中抗生素暴露效应量（OS HR=1.61, PFS HR=1.43, ORR RR=0.58）及时间窗特异性数据（P0081）\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"access_id\": \"source_materials[24].study_summary_A\",\n      \"reason\": \"确认 U2 中 PPI 使用与 ICI 生存结局恶化的荟萃分析数据及时窗差异（P0339）\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"access_id\": \"source_materials[23].study_summary_A\",\n      \"reason\": \"验证 U2 中 HCC 人群抗生素使用未显著恶化 ICI 疗效的反面对照数据（P0275）\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"access_id\": \"source_materials[20].study_summary_A\",\n      \"reason\": \"支持 U2 中 PPI 使用者微生物动态轨迹差异及口腔细菌易位机制（P0033）\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"access_id\": \"source_materials[21].study_summary_A\",\n      \"reason\": \"补充 U2 中 5 万名实体瘤患者抗生素暴露系统综述数据（P0236）\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"access_id\": \"source_materials[27].study_summary_A\",\n      \"reason\": \"验证 U2 中抗生素效应在 NSCLC 中依赖 PD-L1 表达水平的分层证据（P0517）\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","reasoning_content":"The user is asking me to act as an autonomous outline material access planner. I need to return only JSON with status being \"access_plan\", \"partial\", or \"no_change\", and optionally include material_requests.\n\nLooking at the current state:\n- Chapter 1 is being worked on with units U1 and U2 being modifiable\n- Units U3 and U4 are read-only\n- The actual_local_body shows substantial content has already been written for sections 1.1 and 1.2\n- The material_catalog shows 32 source_materials, 0 candidate_materials, 38 tool_materials, and 1 candidate_navigation\n\nI need to assess what materials are needed to complete the current writing task. Looking at the chapter_plan:\n\nFor U1 (跨癌种关联图谱):\n- Already has source_handles: P0096, P0146, P0585, P0478\n- Supporting studies include: P0096, P0170, P0015, P0298, P0204, P0289, P0270, P0393, P0364, P0437, P0545, P0565, P0511\n\nFor U2 (外部干扰与宿主背景):\n- Already has source_handles: P0081, P0402, P0585\n- Supporting studies include: P0123, P0157, P0033, P0236, P0266, P0289, P0275, P0339, P0360, P0421, P0517, P0576, P0548\n\nLooking at the actual_local_body, I can see that much of the content has already been written with citations to many of these sources. However, I need to check if there are any materials that haven't been accessed yet that would be needed to complete or verify the current writing.\n\nFrom the material_catalog, I can see which source_materials are available. \n\nI notice several sources haven't been fully accessed yet. P0170 (Enterotype-specific microbial biomarkers), P0015 (gut microbial signature for combination ICB), P0204 (multi-kingdom gut microbiota in HCC), P0270 (gastrointestinal microbiota in mCRPC), P0393 (Multi-Kingdom Gut Microbiome Interaction), P0364 (Functional convergence amid taxonomic variability), P0437 (Gene-level gut microbiome signatures), P0545 (Polish melanoma patients), P0565 (Systematic Review Melanoma), and P0511 (Meta-analysis metastatic melanoma) all appear to be supporting studies that may need verification or deeper access to ensure the claims in the written sections are properly substantiated.\n\nFor the second unit, I'm seeing P0123 (NSCLC microbial signatures), P0157 (Overcoming Resistance Mechanisms), P0033 (Longitudinal gut microbiome changes), P0236 (Systemic antibiotic exposure), P0266 (Antibiotics in Hispanic NSCLC), P0275 (antibiotic use in HCC), P0339 (PPI use meta-analysis), P0360 (antibiotic duration in gynecologic malignancies), P0421 (sarcopenia impact), P0517 (antibiotics effects by PD-L1), and P0548 (Effect of Gut Microbiota on Systemic Immunity) that similarly need attention.\n\nThe tool_materials contain synthesized information about JCOG2007 trial data and FMT trial evidence that could be valuable for cross-referencing claims.\n\nSince the actual_local_body already contains substantial written content with citations, I should verify whether the key claims are properly supported by the source materials. Some sources appear to have study_summary_A and review_planning_B paths available but may not have been fully accessed for their detailed findings. I need to request access to specific materials that would help validate the claims already made in the text.\n\nLooking at what's available in the catalog, I can see several sources have deep_read_material paths that haven't been fully utilized yet. I should prioritize accessing materials that directly support the major claims in sections 1.1 and 1.2, particularly those with source_handles that are cited but whose detailed content hasn't been thoroughly reviewed.\n\nFor the cross-cancer association patterns in U1, I need to verify the specific findings from P0478 regarding the lack of universal biomarkers, check P0015 for how treatment regimens modify microbial signatures, and examine P0270 for the mCRPC data showing A. muciniphila's negative correlation. The multi-kingdom analyses in P0393 and P0204 would strengthen the discussion of microbial diversity across tumor types, while P0545 provides important population-specific data from the Polish melanoma cohort. P0364's functional convergence framework helps explain why taxonomic differences don't necessarily mean functional differences.\n\nFor U2's focus on external干扰 and host background, P0081 and P0402 contain the meta-analysis quantifying antibiotic and PPI effects that I've already referenced, but I should verify the specific effect sizes and time windows. P0339 offers additional PPI meta-analysis data, P0236 provides large-scale antibiotic exposure data across 50k+ patients, and P0275 presents the important HCC counterexample where antibiotics showed no significant effect. P0033's longitudinal data would help establish temporal relationships between microbial changes and treatment response.\n\nI should prioritize accessing materials that directly support the specific claims already made in the text, focusing on those with available deep_read_material or local_passages paths that haven't been fully utilized yet.","role":"assistant"},"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"logprobs":null}],"object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":46443,"completion_tokens":1962,"total_tokens":48405,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1301,"text_tokens":1962},"prompt_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":46443}},"created":1791262141,"system_fingerprint":null,"model":"qwen3.5-plus","id":"chatcmpl-ea94aceb-35ef-981b-ae44-6b5fe6c34597"}